# Terminal Commands

## Build Commands
```bash
# Compile TypeScript
npm run compile

# Compile extensions only
npm run gulp compile-extensions

# Build full application (macOS ARM64)
npm run gulp vscode-darwin-arm64

# Watch mode
npm run watch
```

## Extension Development
```bash
# Install extension dependencies
cd extensions/coauthor-agent && npm install

# Compile single extension
cd extensions/coauthor-agent && npm run compile

# Package extension
cd extensions/coauthor-agent && npm run package
```

## Testing (Comprehensive)

VS Code uses layered testing. Test incrementally, not just at the end.

```bash
# Quick TypeScript check (no emit)
cd extensions/coauthor-agent && npx tsc --noEmit

# Full core compilation
npm run compile -- --max-old-space-size=4096

# Compile single extension
npm run gulp compile-extension:coauthor-agent

# Run extension in development host
# Press F5 in VS Code with extension folder open

# Run unit tests
npm test

# Run integration tests
./scripts/test-integration.sh
```

### Gate Testing Commands
```bash
# GATE 1: Scaffold valid
cd extensions/coauthor-agent && npm install && npx tsc --noEmit

# GATE 2: Extension compiles
cd extensions/coauthor-agent && npm run compile
ls -la dist/extension.js

# GATE 3: In bundle
npm run gulp compile-extension:coauthor-agent
```

## Common Issues
- If `npm install` fails, try `npm install --legacy-peer-deps`
- If gulp tasks fail, ensure you're in the repository root
- If extension doesn't load, check `package.json` activation events
